/*
  PLAIN-TEXT SCREENPLAY TEMPLATE — Fountain format (https://fountain.io)

  Fountain is ordinary text that screenplay apps (Highland, Beat, Slugline,
  Afterwriting, Fade In, etc.) render as a correctly formatted screenplay.
  Skills in this repo read and write this format, so keep to the rules below.

  Cheat sheet
  - Scene heading:     a line starting with INT. / EXT. / INT./EXT. / EST.
                       (or force one with a leading dot: .FLASHBACK)
                       Optional scene number at the end: #1#
  - Action:            any normal paragraph. Present tense, what we SEE and HEAR.
  - Character:         a line in ALL CAPS followed by dialogue on the next line.
                       Extensions: (V.O.) voice-over, (O.S.) off-screen, (CONT'D)
  - Parenthetical:     (quietly) on its own line under the character name.
  - Dual dialogue:     add ^ after the second character's name.
  - Transition:        ALL CAPS ending in TO:   e.g. CUT TO:   or force with >
  - Centered text:     >THE END<
  - Notes:             [[ note to yourself — not printed ]]
  - Sections/synopses: # Act / sequence headers and = one-line synopses
                       (outline only, not printed).
  - Emphasis:          *italic*  **bold**  _underline_
  - Page break:        ===
  - Boneyard:          text between slash-star and star-slash is ignored (like this block).

  Pipeline conventions for this repo
  - One file per episode: script/ep01.fountain, script/ep02.fountain …
  - Scene numbers (#1#, #2# …) must match the shot list IDs (EP01_SC01 …).
  - Use [[ ]] notes for directing / look / sound intentions; the shot-list
    skill picks them up.
  - Voice-over lines get an ID in a note, e.g. [[VO01_L001]], so the voice
    skill can generate and track each line.
*/

# ACT ONE

= Mira, alone above the city, notices the car that should not be there.

EXT. ROOFTOP - NIGHT #1#

[[look: night_teal · sound: rain bed, distant traffic, no music]]

Rain needles through the sodium glow. Antennas, a dead neon sign, puddles that hold the whole city upside down.

MIRA (30s, hood up, one hand buried in her pocket) walks to the edge and stops.

MIRA (V.O.)
[[VO01_L001]]
Every night I count the lights. Tonight one of them is missing.

She looks down.

EXT. STREET - CONTINUOUS #2#

Far below, an empty street. A single car glides through the intersection, headlights off.

BACK TO:

EXT. ROOFTOP - NIGHT #3#

Mira steps back from the edge. Her phone buzzes. She doesn't look at it.

MIRA
(to herself)
Not tonight.

The phone keeps buzzing.

TOM (O.S.)
(from the stairwell)
Mira? You up there?

MIRA
Go home, Tom.

TOM (O.S.)
I am home.

MIRA ^
You're not.

She turns. The rooftop door creaks open behind her — nobody there.

SMASH CUT TO:

INT. MIRA'S APARTMENT - NIGHT #4#

[[look: warm tungsten practicals, deep shadows · lens: 35mm static]]

A single lamp. Wet footprints on the floorboards lead *toward* the window, not away from it.

Mira stands in the doorway, dripping.

MIRA
(barely audible)
Who's there?

Silence. Only the fridge hum.

FADE OUT.

===

